  "description": "X-FILES (XFiles / DeerStealer) is a long-running C#-written\ninfostealer first observed on Russian hacker forums in March\n2021. Later evolutions (2024+) are sold under the rebranded name\nDeerStealer by the same actor on dark-web forums and Telegram\nwith a tiered subscription model. Targets Chromium and Gecko\nbrowsers, 80+ browser-based crypto wallet extensions, plus\nVPN, FTP, RDP, and messenger client data.",
  "aliases": [
    "X-FILES",
    "DeerStealer",
    "X-Files Stealer"
  ],
  "typical_targets": [
    "Browser saved credentials and cookies (Chromium and Gecko)",
    "80+ browser-based crypto wallet extensions",
    "Crypto wallet desktop clients",
    "VPN, FTP, RDP client configs",
    "Messenger session data (Telegram, Discord, Steam)"
  ],
  "detection_notes": "XFiles `Information.txt` carries the panel banner together with\nvictim hardware and locale fields. Older 2021-2022 variants and\nthe rebranded 2024+ DeerStealer share the same field set so the\nfamily rule covers both eras. An aggregator-stripped variant\nredistributed via the Cloud WLFR project (`t.me/WichLoveFromR`,\n`linktr.ee/WLFRcloud`, support `@AltairSupport`) drops the\n`Operation ID:` panel-run identifier but keeps the rest of the\nXFiles-canonical field set; the structural fingerprint covers both\nshapes.",
